    <string name="helper_row_desc">Draws the island above status bar icons, and hides it in apps you choose and while you type</string>
    <string name="helper_disclosure_title">Turn on the helper?</string>
    <string name="helper_disclosure_body">The helper is an accessibility service. Notch Island uses it for two things only: to draw the island above the status bar, so notification icons go under it instead of across it, and to learn which app is in front and whether a keyboard or the notification shade is open, so the island can step out of the way. It does not read what is on your screen, and nothing is stored or sent anywhere.\n\nOn the next screen, find Notch Island helper and switch it on. If Android says it is a restricted setting, tap App info below, open the ⋮ menu, choose Allow restricted settings, and try again.</string>
